# check: fail error[E8a, E4a]: this shift is past its literal's width, and nothing adapts it to a wider type
# E4a/E8a: "1 << 40" adapted to an I64 is computed exactly; with nothing adapting it, it is an I32 shift by 40, which
# E8a leaves undefined - so it is an error, as a written amount past a typed value's width is
fn main() ? {
    t := $(1 << 40)
}
